'' 'tiko metadata' WITH AN ERROR IN THE GRAPH (exit 1) still reports what is known: the
'' modules that resolved -- 'empty' has no source, and 'ext', found after it, keeps its own
'' files -- the search paths, and each unit's defines and include directories. An editor's
'' project is often half-written.
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TKO_MODCACHE=build/.bmb/cache
'' CLEAN: build/.bmb
'' ARGS: metadata -target windows-x86_64 --manifest tests/driver/src/build-metabroken
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: "modules":[{"chain":"empty","package":"empty","dir":"tests/driver/src/build-metabroken/lib/empty","files":[],"imports":[]}
'' EXPECT-OUT: {"chain":"ext","package":"ext","dir":"tests/driver/src/build-metabroken/lib/ext","files":["tests/driver/src/build-metabroken/lib/ext/ext.tiko"],"imports":[]}
'' EXPECT-OUT: "searchPaths":{"roots":["tests/driver/src/build-metabroken/lib"]
'' EXPECT-OUT: "defines":["GREETING=1"],"includes":["tests/driver/src/build-metabroken/lib"
